Date: Wed, 17 Oct 2018 13:22:23 +0000
Subject: Re: Asymptotic covariance matrix of functions of parameters
Message-ID: <skgZRyzqtYM.I6ULGtLLBAAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <skgZRyzqtYM.vGve-_7WlEgJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
References: <skgZRyzqtYM.vGve-_7WlEgJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/skgZRyzqtYM/m/I6ULGtLLBAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In lavaan dev 0.6-4.1337 (or higher), lavInspect(fit, "vcov.def.joint")
will return the *joint* variance matrix of both the free parameters and
the defined parameters.

To follow up on the example, this is how it is done:

set.seed(1234)
X <- rnorm(100)
M <- 0.5*X + rnorm(100)
Y <- 0.7*M + rnorm(100)
Data <- data.frame(X = X, Y = Y, M = M)
model <- ' # direct effect
              Y ~ c*X
            # mediator
              M ~ a*X
              Y ~ b*M
            # indirect effect (a*b)
              ab := a*b
            # total effect
              total := c + (a*b)'
fit <- sem(model, data = Data)

# first get ordinary vcov
VCOV <- vcov(fit)

# extract free parameters

x <- coef(fit)

# compute jacobian for 'defined parameters'

JAC <- numDeriv:::jacobian(func = fit@Mod...@def.function, x = x)

# add identity matrix for free parameters
JAC2 <- rbind(diag(nrow = ncol(JAC)), JAC)
VCOV.joint <- JAC2 %*% VCOV %*% t(JAC2)

Yves.

